                                {
                                    "id": "ghrpbc",
                                    "elType": "widget",
                                    "widgetType": "text-editor",
                                    "settings": {
                                        "editor": "<p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#3D4F66\"><a href=\"https://www.biopentra.eu/\" style=\"color:#1F5FAE;text-decoration:none\">Home</a> &gt; Resources &gt; Growth Hormone Releasing Peptides</p>",
                                        "text_color": "#3D4F66"
                                    },
                                    "elements": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "id": "ghrpH1",
                                    "elType": "widget",
                                    "widgetType": "heading",
                                    "settings": {
                                        "header_size": "h1",
                                        "title": "Growth Hormone Releasing Peptides",
                                        "title_color": "#0F1F33"
                                    },
                                    "elements": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "id": "ghrpintro",
                                    "elType": "widget",
                                    "widgetType": "text-editor",
                                    "settings": {
                                        "editor": "<p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#3D4F66\">Growth hormone releasing peptides (GHRPs) are a family of research compounds often discussed together because they are studied in similar laboratory contexts. In broad terms, they are peptide-based materials examined for how they interact with endocrine signaling pathways, particularly those connected to growth hormone-related receptor activity.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#3D4F66\">Researchers may group these compounds when comparing receptor interaction patterns, peptide signaling behavior, or pathway models in controlled settings. The category is useful for organizing literature and catalog information, even when individual compounds differ in structure and reported laboratory focus.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#3D4F66\">On a research storefront, GHRP pages serve a practical role: they connect related catalog entries, explain shared terminology, and point to handling guidance that applies across lyophilized peptide materials. Readers can use this overview before reviewing individual product listings or adjacent resource pages.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#3D4F66\">This page is an informational resource from BioPentra. It is intended to support understanding of how GHRP-related research compounds are commonly categorized and referenced in a research-use context. It does not describe medical applications or use outside qualified laboratory work.</p>",
                                        "text_color": "#3D4F66"
                                    },
                                    "elements": []
                                }
                            ],
                            "isInner": true
                        }
